<section class="panel" aria-label="Original 2021 Grade3 Unit5 Lesson10 equivalent fractions first-party teaching"><h2>Equivalent Fractions</h2>
<p>Original choral count: 1/2,2/2; 3/2,4/2; 5/2,6/2; 7/2,8/2. Compare the previous count to 16/4.</p>
<h3>Six original source shape choices — semantic equivalents, not publisher artwork</h3>
<table class="source-chart"><thead><tr><th>Original item</th><th>Shaded area</th><th>One half?</th></tr></thead><tbody>
<tr><th scope="row">A</th><td>2/4</td><td>Yes</td></tr>
<tr><th scope="row">B</th><td>3/4</td><td>No</td></tr>
<tr><th scope="row">C</th><td>1/2</td><td>Yes</td></tr>
<tr><th scope="row">D</th><td>2/4</td><td>Yes</td></tr>
<tr><th scope="row">E</th><td>1/2</td><td>Yes</td></tr>
<tr><th scope="row">F</th><td>1/4</td><td>No</td></tr>
</tbody></table><p>Source-correct: <strong>A, C, D, E</strong>. In original F there are two UNEQUAL pieces: only a quarter of the whole is shaded; no auto-grade without inspecting equal area.</p>
